,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & w & v \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2v & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(2v-0) \\\\  & =2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2v & =0 \\\\ v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $v=0$ defines the plane $v=0,$ i.e., $uw$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406803 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406801 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406803 #edb/ref 1069 "q-39710" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406803 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406803 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}+vw,\\,y=2-uv,\\,z={v}^{2}-w.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406803 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9eac1497-79c1-5ed3-be68-00cfa0edfef5" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406803 #edb/ref 1074 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =2v & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & w & v \\\\ -v & -u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u(-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}-u & 0 \\\\ 2v & -1\\end{aligned}|+(-v)(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}w & v \\\\ 2v & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u(u-0)+v(-w-2{v}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}-2{v}^{3}-vw.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585]}
